.TH XTC_SCHED 3 "2026" "libxtc" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
xtc_sched_policy_set, xtc_sched_continuous_set, xtc_sched_get_stats \- optional runtime lane policies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <xtc_sched.h>

int xtc_sched_policy_set(xtc_loop_t *loop,
    const xtc_sched_policy_t *policy);
int xtc_sched_continuous_set(xtc_loop_t *loop, uint32_t max_bypass);
int xtc_sched_get_stats(xtc_loop_t *loop, xtc_sched_stats_t *out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build with --enable-sched-policy (Meson: -Dsched_policy=true).
The default build exposes these entry points but returns XTC_E_NOSYS.
An enabled build without an installed policy retains the ordinary picker,
queue order, and weighted runtime accounting.
.PP
Initialize policy.size to sizeof(policy), policy.version to
XTC_SCHED_VERSION (1), max_bypass to a positive uint32_t, and select to a
non-NULL callback. ran is optional. The descriptor is copied; callback code
and user context are borrowed through loop teardown. NULL removes the policy.
Installation/removal is setup-only: the first run or single step, even an
empty step, freezes configuration permanently. Setup must be externally serialized before execution starts; concurrent
lifecycle destruction is not supported.
.PP
select receives a callback-lifetime immutable xtc_sched_view_t array, ordered
by numeric lane ID. Only ready lanes appear: -1 is the default FIFO/deque;
0 through 15 identify existing class queues. Each lane contains shares,
runs (quanta served under the policy), and bypasses (consecutive ready
selection opportunities without service). The uint32_t ready and active
fields provide advisory batch counts, or zero for unregistered lanes and the
default lane. Active includes blocked batch members; it is not readiness.
Hints never add a lane to the snapshot. No task or queue pointer is exposed.
Return a ready lane ID or XTC_SCHED_DEFAULT (-2) to use the ordinary picker.
Invalid choices fall back. A default-deque steal race also falls back without
calling select again or hiding runnable class work.
.PP
The runtime overrides preferences when a continuously ready lane reaches
max_bypass, choosing the greatest bypass count with stable numeric tie breaks.
Counters saturate; empty or serviced lanes reset their age. With L ready lanes,
service occurs within max_bypass + L opportunities, assuming callbacks and
dispatched tasks return. This is not a wall-time bound, preemption, or a
per-task fairness guarantee for the default LIFO deque. Custom mode may
reorder weighted shares; it does not promise exact proportional CPU shares.
.PP
The optional ran callback receives the selected lane BEFORE a proc can
change its class, units equal to one, and verdict XTC_SCHED_DONE,
XTC_SCHED_YIELD, or XTC_SCHED_PARK. A pending result consumed by a latched wake
is normalized to YIELD. Quantum counts are not CPU time.
.PP
Callbacks must be bounded, nonblocking, allocation-free, deterministic under
simulation, and must not yield or mutate runtime state. Configuration from
callbacks is rejected. The runtime owns all queues, task lifetimes, and wakes.
.PP
Initialize out.size and out.version before xtc_sched_get_stats. Read only from
the owner or while quiescent. The snapshot reports selections (callback
invocations), fallbacks, invalid_choices, and fairness_overrides. No policy
means zero policy counters. Counters saturate at UINT64_MAX.
.SH CONTINUOUS BATCH POLICY
xtc_sched_continuous_set installs the built-in continuous batch-lane policy
with a positive max_bypass. It uses loop-owned context, allocates nothing,
and has the same pre-first-step installation restriction as policy_set.
Passing NULL to policy_set removes it before execution starts.
.PP
Among registered batch classes present in the real ready-lane snapshot with
a nonzero ready hint, prefer the greatest bypass age. Equal ages rotate by
class ID after actual class service. No clocks or application pointers
participate in ordering. The mandatory runtime fairness guard still applies
to all ready lanes, including ordinary tasks and the default lane.
.PP
With no eligible batch class, the policy returns XTC_SCHED_DEFAULT and defers
to the ordinary picker, subject to that same fairness guard. An active but
blocked group does not manufacture readiness or receive batch preference.
Each explicit class supports at most one batch group on its owner loop;
ordinary tasks may share that class. Groups using the NULL/default class
remain supported by the batch engine but have no continuous-policy preference.
The policy selects a class, not an individual group member, and does not
change the class FIFO. Batch iteration and membership remain the engine's
responsibility and work without this policy.
.SH RETURN VALUES
XTC_OK on success; XTC_E_NOSYS when disabled; XTC_E_INVAL for NULL required
arguments, wrong descriptor size, missing select, or zero max_bypass;
XTC_E_VERSION for unknown version; XTC_E_AGAIN for installation after start
or while another installer holds the descriptor. Size is checked before version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xtc_loop (3),
.BR xtc_exec (3)
